cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "LumenNet: Deep Learning Low-Light Image Enhancement"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Oliinyk"
    given-names: "Leonid"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-9392-2271"
  - family-names: "Lall"
    given-names: "Sara"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-05-13
abstract: "LumenNet is a deep learning-based image enhancement pipeline designed to recover structural details and accurate colors from underexposed, low-light photographs. It utilizes a U-Net architecture with a ResNet18 backbone, operating conceptually within the LAB color space to preserve chromaticity while enhancing luminance. The system is deployed as a microservice architecture with a FastAPI backend and a Gradio frontend."
keywords:
  - "deep learning"
  - "image enhancement"
  - "low-light"
  - "computer vision"
  - "onnx"
license: "MIT"
repository-code: "https://github.com/leo-oli/lumennet"
